ics in live neonatal rat cardiac myocytes reveals distinct functions of compartmentalized phosphodiesterases. <source>Circ. Res.</source> <volume>95</volume>:<fpage>67</fpage>&#x02013;75.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15178638</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Mongillo, M., C.G. Tocchetti, A. Terrin, V. Lissandron, Y.F. Cheung, W.R. Dostmann, T. Pozzan, D.A. Kass, N. Paolocci, M.D. Houslay, and M. Zaccolo. <year>2006</year>. Compartmentalized phosphodiesterase-2 activity blunts beta-adrenergic cardiac inotropy via an NO/cGMP-dependent pathway. <source>Circ. Res.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>226</fpage>&#x02013;234.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16357307</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Nikolaev, V.O., M. Bunemann, L. Hein, A. Hannawacker, and M.J. Lohse. <year>2004</year>. Novel single chain cAMP sensors for receptor-induced signal propagation. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>37215</fpage>&#x02013;37218.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15231839</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Perry, S.J., G.S. Baillie, T.A. Kohout, I. McPhee, M.M. Magiera, K.L. Ang, W.E. Miller, A.J. McLean, M. Conti, M.D. Houslay, and R.J. Lefkowitz. <year>2002</year>. Targeting of cyclic AMP degradation to beta 2-adrenergic receptors by beta-arrestins. <source>Science.</source> <volume>298</volume>:<fpage>834</fpage>&#x02013;836.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12399592</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Ponsioen, B., J. Zhao, J. Riedl, F. Zwartkruis, G. van der Krogt, M. Zaccolo, W.H. Moolenaar, J.L. Bos, and K. Jalink. <year>2004</year>. Detecting cAMP-induced Epac activation by fluorescence resonance energy transfer: Epac as a novel cAMP indicator. <source>EMBO Rep.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>1176</fpage>&#x02013;1180.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15550931</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citat